    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d290-a1">

                <pb facs="0568" n="498" xml:id="pg498"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Headquarters District of Montana</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Helena, Mont.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-03-23"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 23,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Adjutant-General</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Department Dakota, Fort Snelling, Minn.:</hi></p>
                <p>Following received: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p rendition="#right">“<hi rendition="#small-caps">Fort Benton</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">March</hi> 22, 1883.</p>
                        <p>“Large war party Crees fighting herders and Piegans at Kipp’s, on Marias
                            19th. Stole forty horses, killed nine work cattle, two Piegans, and
                            several horses. Two Crees killed: moving towards Walsh. Can’t you have
                            them intercepted?</p>
                        <p rendition="#right">“J. G. BAKER &amp; CO.,</p>
                        <p rendition="#right">“T. C. POWER &amp; BROS., and others.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Orders were sent on receipt of the above dispatch to Fort Assinnihoine for the
                    cavalry to try to intercept the Crees. The commanding officer at Assinniboine
                    was also directed to communicate as to the matter with the commanding officer at
                    Fort Walsh.</p>
                <closer><signed>RUGER,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Commanding
                        District.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>(Mail Bismarck.)</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
